  message: "Fixed in PR (dev e1b4e10b7c).\n\nBehavioral evidence: `hypergumbo verify-claims` on merged dev with the item's claim (source_taint untrusted_input, prohibited_sink_zone subprocess) and `subprocess.run(body, shell=True)` after each of:\n  body = urllib.request.urlopen(url).read()                   -> violated (dev before: confirmed_with_caveats)\n  body = urllib.request.build_opener().open(url).read()       -> violated (dev before: confirmed_with_caveats)\n  s = socket.create_connection((h, 80)); body = s.recv(1024)  -> violated (dev before: confirmed_with_caveats)\nThe before-verdicts were measured on a dev worktree in the same session. Production-path tests are test_http_response_receive_surface.py and test_py_member_return_types.py.\n\nFix:\n- library_signatures: urlopen / OpenerDirector.open / HTTP(S)Connection.getresponse -> http.client.HTTPResponse, and socket.create_connection -> socket.socket. Only the http(s) type is used; addinfourl for file:/data:/ftp: is deliberately not typed.\n- py.py: a member called on a typed receiver is typed from its signature row (_member_return_type); a `with` item from a typed receiver is typed the same way.\n- io_primitives: HTTPResponse's read family, header/url/status accessors and begin are net_recv. Its 28-member public surface is enumerated complete, and the scope gate admits it.\n\nCorpus A/B (the item required one: a new source), classified crossings vs dev:\n  django +17 (HTTPResponse read 11, getheader 5, info 1)\n  superset +6\n  feast 0\nNone lost. 16 of 16 sampled sites are real HTTP response reads (django TemplateCommand.download, test-client getresponse() reads, superset report fetches).\n\nPorted from the unmerged draft 206e733d13. Its WI-patit half (returns_handle; opener sends stay clean) was deliberately EXCLUDED. That item is separate and still todo_hard, and its ruling is on record only as an agent-relayed note; WI-dibit's opener pin test is unchanged."  # a6b1
